const rawSourceContent = "Key Takeaways\r\nUnderstanding Adult Mental Health & Emotional Wellbeing\r\nImportance of Mental Health in Everyday Life\r\nStress, Anxiety, Depression & Low Mood\r\nBurnout & Emotional Exhaustion\r\nSleep Problems & Insomnia\r\nOCD, Intrusive Thoughts & Panic Attacks\r\nRelationship & Emotional Wellbeing\r\nCareer Pressure & Work-Life Balance\r\nMind-Body Connection & Overall Wellbeing\r\nSigns You Should Not Ignore\r\nHealthy Lifestyle & Stress Management\r\nComprehensive Adult Mental Health Assessment\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nPersonalised Emotional Wellbeing Guidance\r\nEmotional Resilience & Healthy Coping Strategies\r\nLong-Term Mental Wellness Support\r\nFAQs About Adult Mental Health Care\r\n\r\n\r\nAdult Mental Health\r\n\r\nAdult Mental Health Care & Emotional Wellbeing Support in India\r\n\r\nSupporting Emotional Health, Mental Resilience and Overall Wellbeing Through Every Stage of Adult Life\r\n\r\nOpportunities, responsibilities and challenges experienced in adult life impact emotional wellbeing over time. Careers and relationships, marriage and parenting, financial matters, health issues and one's personal expectations can sometimes be overwhelmingly emotional. Normal stress is one of the various occurrences of life, while mental health issues that are not going away and require attention and appropriate support. [1]\r\n\r\nMental health is the opposite of mental illness. It impacts on adults' thought patterns, emotions, decision making, relationships, coping, work performance and quality of life. Emotional wellbeing is crucial for someone to face life challenges, get over setbacks and grow as a person and in their career. [1]\r\n\r\nMany adults have concerns like chronic stress, anxiety, depression, burn out, sleep issues, over thinking, panic attacks, and emotional exhaustion or relationship issues that go undetected. These concerns may have begun slowly and have been overlooked until they start to impact the person's ability to function, daily activities, physical health, or family life. [1][2]\r\n\r\nAdult mental health is shaped by a number of interrelated factors such as brain health, sleep, nutrition, lifestyle habits, emotional resilience, relationships and physical wellbeing – at Manovaidya, we believe this. We do not just deal with symptoms – we want to know the full emotional picture for each person. [1][3]\r\n\r\nWe are led by Dr. Ankush Garg, the Mental Health Specialist and Founder of Manovaidya, who is a practitioner of Neuro-Ayurveda Development System, which is a 5-pillar model that includes a holistic approach to mental wellbeing support, comprehensive assessment and personalised guidance to support adults develop healthier, balanced lives.\r\n \r\n\r\nAdult Mental Health Areas We Support\r\n\r\nAll adults are unique. Emotional issues can occur due to work, family, health, relationships or personal issues.\r\n\r\nOur Adult Mental Health Care includes support for:\r\n\r\nStress & Anxiety\r\n\r\nKnowing what worry, high levels of stress, excessive thinking and anxiety look like that affect daily functioning.\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Anxiety Support\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nDepression & Low Mood\r\n\r\nSupport for persistent sadness, reduced motivation, emotional withdrawal and loss of interest in everyday activities.\r\n\r\nLearn More → Depression & Low Mood\r\n\r\n\r\nSleep Problems & Insomnia\r\n\r\nBeing familiar with sleep problems that impact emotional health, energy and health generally. [4]\r\n \r\nLearn More → Sleep Disorders & Insomnia\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nBurnout & Emotional Exhaustion\r\n \r\nSupporting adults to understand the problems of 'burnout', emotional fatigue and long-term stress at work. [2]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Burnout Support\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nOCD & Intrusive Thoughts\r\n\r\n\r\nSupport for obsessive thoughts, compulsive behaviours and intrusive thinking patterns.\r\n\r\n Learn More → OCD Support\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nPanic Attacks & Panic Disorder\r\n \r\nHelping individuals understand sudden episodes of intense fear, panic attacks and their impact on daily life.\r\n \r\nLearn More → Panic Disorder Support\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nRelationship & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\nEmotional support for life transitions, friendships and marriage and/or family relationships.\r\n\r\nLearn More → Relationship Support\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\nStress Management & Mind-Body Balance\r\n\r\nSupport adults to understand the link between emotional wellbeing and physical health and the importance of adopting healthy lifestyle habits. [1][3]\r\n \r\nLearn More → Stress Management & Mind-Body Balance\r\n\r\n\r\nCareer Pressure & Work-Life Balance\r\n \r\nHelp with stress at work, career pressures, employment anxiety and healthier work-life balance. [2]\r\n\r\n\r\nLearn More → Career Pressure Support\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\nPersonal Growth & Emotional Resilience\r\n \r\nSupporting adults to build confidence, coping, emotional regulation and mental health for long-term.\r\n\r\nLearn More → Emotional Resilience Support\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nWhy Adult Mental Health Matters\r\n \r\nThere are almost all aspects of adult life that are impacted by mental wellbeing. The emotional health affects decision making, productivity, relationships, parenting, physical health and quality of sleep and overall life satisfaction. [1]\r\n\r\nHealthy mental wellbeing helps adults: \r\n\r\nManage stress effectively\r\nBuild healthier relationships\r\nEnhance concentration and efficiency of work\r\nMake balanced decisions\r\nAdjust to change in life\r\nStrengthen emotional resilience\r\nKeep physically and emotionally well.\r\n\r\nEarly detection of mental health issues enables people to access the right help before mental health problems start to impact on day to day life. [1]\r\n \r\n\r\nUnderstanding Adult Mental Health\r\n \r\nMental health is a crucial component of health. It affects adults' thinking, feelings, behaviour, decision making, emotional regulation and coping with life. [1]\r\n \r\nAs we grow up as adults, we go through the phases of life with their own opportunities and responsibilities. Emotional wellbeing can be affected as people start a career, manage relationships, have children, look after elderly parents, take care of their finances and cope with life changes.\r\n \r\nIt is normal to feel stressed, worried or down at times. If these feelings persist, are overwhelming or start to impact on work, relationships or daily functioning, however, it is important that they are discussed and suitably professional directed. [1]\r\n \r\nSupporting adult mental health is not just about coping with emotional challenges and difficulties; it's about being resilient and improving emotional balance and wellbeing throughout life. [1]\r\n \r\n\r\nCommon Adult Mental Health Concerns\r\n \r\nEach adult has their own unique experience. Some may have one emotional issue or more than one emotional issue that impacts several areas of life.\r\n \r\nStress & Anxiety\r\n \r\nThere are often constant demands in modern life for work, money, relationships and family.\r\n\r\n\r\nSome adults may experience:\r\n\r\n\r\nPersistent worrying\r\nDifficulty relaxing\r\nOverthinking\r\nRestlessness\r\nPhysical tension\r\nDifficulty concentrating\r\n \r\nPracticing healthy strategies of stress management can help to support emotional wellness.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Stress & Anxiety\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nDepression & Low Mood\r\n \r\nEmotional wellbeing and quality of life could be impaired by persistent sadness, decreased motivation or loss of interest in activities. [1]\r\n \r\nAdults may have:\r\n\r\nLow mood\r\nEmotional withdrawal\r\nReduced motivation\r\nFatigue\r\nDifficulty enjoying activities\r\nAny symptoms that are ongoing should always be assessed professionally. [1]\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Depression & Low Mood\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nBurnout & Emotional Exhaustion\r\n \r\nEmotional exhaustion can be caused by long term stress at work or caring for another person, or by continuous workplace demands. [2]\r\n\r\nThese can include:\r\n\r\nConstant fatigue\r\nFeeling emotionally drained\r\nReduced motivation\r\nDifficulty concentrating\r\nFeeling overwhelmed\r\nRecognising burnout early may help prevent further emotional strain.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Burnout Support\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSleep Problems & Insomnia\r\n\r\nSleep is a big part of emotional health, memory, focus and physical health. [4]\r\n \r\nWhen adults have poor sleep they might feel:\r\n \r\nDifficulty falling asleep\r\nFrequent waking during the night\r\nEarly morning awakening\r\nDaytime tiredness\r\nReduced concentration\r\n\r\nIf sleep difficulties continue, healthy sleep habits and advice from a professional might help.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Sleep Problems\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPanic Attacks\r\n\r\nSome adults may have suddenly intense feelings of anxiety or discomfort which can include physical symptoms.\r\n\r\nThese episodes can include:\r\n\r\nRapid heartbeat\r\nSweating\r\nShortness of breath\r\nDizziness\r\nFeeling out of control\r\n\r\nA professional assessment will help to identify the underlying reasons and support that is needed.\r\n\r\nRead about Panic Disorder on the website.\r\n\r\n\r\nObsessive Thoughts & Compulsive Behaviours (OCD)\r\n\r\nOthers have persistent intrusive thoughts or repetitive behaviours that become uncontrollable and disruptive.\r\n\r\nProfessional evaluation can be beneficial in understanding these experiences and offering the right care.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About OCD\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRelationship Challenges\r\n\r\nRelationships influence emotional wellbeing throughout adulthood.\r\n\r\nDisabilities can affect some adults in the following ways:\r\n\r\nMarriage\r\nParenting\r\nFamily relationships\r\nFriendships\r\nWorkplace relationships\r\nEmotional communication\r\n\r\nSupportive relationships are important and require good communication and understanding of emotions.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Relationship & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\n\r\nCareer Pressure & Work-Life Balance\r\n\r\nEmotional stress can sometimes occur in the professional setting. [2]\r\n\r\nAdults may experience:\r\n\r\nHigh work pressure\r\nDifficulty balancing work and family\r\nCareer uncertainty\r\nWorkplace conflicts\r\nReduced job satisfaction\r\n\r\nBetter coping skills can help to enhance emotional health and work performance.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Career Pressure Support\r\n\r\n\r\nMind-Body Balance\r\n\r\nThe feelings side of life and the health side of life are intertwined. [1][3]\r\n\r\nStress can have a long-term effect on:\r\n\r\nSleep quality\r\nEnergy levels\r\nAppetite\r\nDigestion\r\nMuscle tension\r\nOverall wellbeing\r\n\r\nEmotional and physical health are treated together and a more balanced lifestyle is encouraged.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Mind-Body Balance\r\n\r\n\r\nSigns You Should Not Ignore\r\n\r\n\r\nLife naturally involves some changes in mood. But if there is a continuing worry, this is one that needs to be taken seriously and addressed in a manner that has a positive impact on everyday life. [1]\r\n\r\nIf you see any of the following, you might benefit from a professional mental health assessment:\r\n\r\n\r\nEmotional Changes\r\nPersistent sadness\r\nConstant anxiety or worry\r\nIrritability\r\nFeeling emotionally overwhelmed\r\nLoss of motivation\r\n\r\nBehavioural Changes\r\n\r\nWithdrawal from family or friends\r\nAvoiding social situations\r\nDifficulty managing emotions\r\nReduced interest in daily activities\r\nIncreased reliance on unhealthy coping habits\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWork & Productivity\r\n\r\nDifficulty concentrating\r\nReduced productivity\r\nPoor decision-making\r\nFrequent absenteeism\r\nFeeling unable to manage everyday responsibilities\r\n\r\nPhysical Changes\r\n\r\nPoor sleep\r\nPersistent fatigue\r\nAppetite changes\r\nFrequent headaches\r\nMuscle tension\r\nDigestive discomfort\r\n\r\n\r\nThe presence of any physical symptoms that have been ongoing should also be checked by a trained health care worker.\r\n\r\nRelationship Difficulties\r\n\r\nFrequent conflicts\r\nDifficulty communicating\r\nEmotional distance\r\nFeeling isolated\r\nReduced interest in relationships\r\n\r\n\r\nHow Adult Mental Health Affects Everyday Life\r\n\r\nMental wellbeing has an impact on many aspects of adult life. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\nHealthy emotional wellbeing supports:\r\n\r\nBetter decision-making\r\nStronger relationships\r\nImproved work performance\r\nGreater resilience\r\nHealthy parenting\r\nBetter sleep\r\nPhysical wellbeing\r\nOverall quality of life\r\n\r\nIf the emotional needs are not met then there is a risk that this will impact upon personal, professional and social wellbeing over time. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\nTaking Care of Your Mental Wellbeing\r\n\r\nMental wellbeing is supported through consistent daily habits.\r\n\r\nFor many adults the following is helpful:\r\n\r\nHealthy sleep routines\r\nBalanced nutrition\r\nRegular physical activity\r\nStress management practices\r\nHealthy relationships\r\nMeaningful hobbies\r\nMindfulness and relaxation techniques\r\nSeeking professional support when emotional concerns persist\r\n\r\nAs with physical wellbeing, mental health is a key component of wellbeing, and it is important to take care of ourselves. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\nOur Adult Mental Health Assessment Process\r\n\r\nEach person lives their life in a unique manner. Emotional wellbeing is influenced by personal experiences, relationships, physical health, work responsibilities, lifestyle habits and many other factors. For this reason, it is essential to grasp the whole person, rather than just the individual symptom.\r\n\r\nWe take a holistic approach to understanding your emotional wellbeing, your lifestyle, your behaviour and your mental health at Manovaidya before we can be able to provide you with personalised guidance.\r\n\r\nWe aim to enable the individual to have a clearer understanding of their emotional wellbeing and understand what steps can be taken to enhance their wellbeing in the longer term.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 1 – Understanding Your Concerns\r\n\r\n\r\nAll consultations start with listening.\r\n\r\n\r\nWe make time to listen:\r\n\r\nYour current concerns\r\nEmotional wellbeing\r\nLifestyle habits\r\nSleep patterns\r\nWork and career responsibilities\r\nFamily and relationship dynamics\r\nMedical history\r\nPrevious mental health support, if any\r\n\r\nUnderstanding your personal experiences helps us create a more complete picture of your mental wellbeing.\r\n\r\nStep 2 – Comprehensive Mental Health Assessment\r\n\r\nThere is a structured assessment that looks at a number of factors which could impact emotional wellbeing.\r\n\r\n\r\nThese include:\r\n\r\nStress and anxiety\r\nMood\r\nEmotional resilience\r\nBehaviour patterns\r\nSleep quality\r\nRelationships\r\nWork-life balance\r\nLifestyle habits\r\nCognitive functioning\r\nOverall mental wellbeing\r\n\r\nThis evaluation will be able to highlight strengths and areas for development.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 3 – Understanding Your Emotional Wellbeing Profile\r\n\r\nOnce the assessment is completed, we clearly and practically relate the observations.\r\n\r\nThis includes:\r\n\r\nEmotional strengths\r\nCurrent challenges\r\nFactors that could be contributing to lifestyle\r\nPersonalised recommendations\r\nHealthy coping strategies\r\nNext steps for ongoing support\r\n\r\nWe want people to know who they are and make choices for their emotional health.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Neuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, mental health is seen as a condition of the adult and is approached as a structured system of 5 pillars: Neuro-Ayurveda Development System, which integrates emotional, biological and lifestyle factors. [5][6]\r\n\r\nThis strategy considers the brain-body-behaviour relationship and everyday lifestyle in relation to emotional symptoms and addresses mental wellbeing. [3][5]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Brain Nourishment System\r\n\r\nA healthy brain function is important to support:\r\n\r\nAttention\r\nMemory\r\nDecision-making\r\nEmotional regulation\r\nConcentration\r\nMental resilience\r\n\r\nThis pillar is about supporting healthy brain functions as part of emotional wellbeing.\r\n\r\n2. Gut Response System\r\n\r\nThe gut-brain axis is the bidirectional communication between the two organs all the time. [3][4]\r\n\r\nThis pillar takes a holistic perspective and views healthy nutrition, digestion and gut health as part of the person's physical and emotional health. [3]\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Neural Network System\r\n\r\nHealthy thinking patterns continue to develop in adults through learning and experience.\r\nThis pillar is about improving strength:\r\n\r\nCognitive flexibility\r\nHealthy thinking habits\r\nLearning\r\nEmotional adaptability\r\nProblem-solving\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Sensory Integration System\r\n\r\nThere are many ways our thinking, feeling and responding are impacted by our environment.\r\n\r\nThis pillar reflects sensory experiences and lifestyle factors which could affect stress, emotional regulation and wellbeing.\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Behaviour Guidance System\r\n\r\nActions can be a response to emotional experiences rather than just repetition of behaviour.\r\n\r\nThis pillar allows persons to become aware of patterns of behaviour, create better coping mechanisms and learn positive lifestyle adjustments that will promote long-term mental health.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHow We Support Adults\r\n\r\nAll people have unique experiences, strengths and challenges.\r\n\r\nThe support we provide at Manovaidya is personalised, depending on each person's emotional wellbeing and overall mental health.\r\n\r\nOur approach may include:\r\n\r\nAssessment of mental health in Adults\r\nIndividualized emotional support suggestions\r\nLifestyle Recommendations\r\nStress Management Strategies\r\nBehaviour Guidance\r\nHealthy Routine Planning\r\nMind-Body Balance Support\r\nEmotional Resilience Building\r\nProgress Monitoring and Follow Up\r\n\r\n\r\nWe aim to support people to develop healthier emotional habits, develop resilience and sustain mental wellbeing over the long-term.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy People Across India Choose Manovaidya\r\n\r\nPeople and families from Delhi, Noida, Gurgaon, Faridabad, Ghaziabad, and all over India choose Manovaidya for our structured, holistic and personalized approach to mental health.\r\n\r\nWe are trusted by people for:\r\n\r\nComplete Adult Mental Health Assessments\r\nPersonalised Emotional Wellbeing Guidance\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nHolistic Mind-Body Approach\r\nOnline & In-Clinic Consultations\r\nLong-Term Mental Wellness Support\r\nInsight from Dr. Ankush Garg\r\n\r\nWe aim to increase the awareness of each person of their emotional health and to help them find healthier ways to cope with life's situations.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout Dr. Ankush Garg\r\n\r\nMental Health Specialist & Founder of Manovaidya\r\n\r\nDr. Ankush Garg is the Founder of Manovaidya and the developer of the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\nHis work focuses on helping individuals understand the relationship between emotional wellbeing, brain health, lifestyle, behaviour and overall wellness.\r\n\r\nThrough structured assessments, personalised guidance and continuous follow-up, Dr. Ankush Garg supports adults experiencing stress, anxiety, emotional challenges and other mental health concerns while promoting healthy coping skills and long-term wellbeing.\r\n\r\nBased in Delhi NCR, he provides online and in-clinic consultations for individuals across India.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBook an Adult Mental Health Assessment\r\n\r\nLooking for Professional Mental Health Support?\r\n\r\n\r\nIf stress, anxiety, low mood, burnout, sleep problems or emotional challenges are affecting your daily life, seeking support early can help you better understand your emotional wellbeing and explore appropriate next steps. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we provide structured Adult Mental Health Assessments, personalised guidance and holistic emotional wellbeing support through the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\nTake the First Step Towards Better Mental Wellbeing\r\n\r\nMental health is an important part of overall health. Understanding your emotional wellbeing today can help you build healthier habits, stronger resilience and a better quality of life for the future. [1]\r\n\r\nBook Your Adult Mental Health Assessment Today\r\n\r\n📞 Book Consultation\r\n📞 Talk to Our Team\r\n📞 Schedule Mental Health Assessment\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions About Adult Mental Health Care\r\n\r\n\r\n1. What is adult mental health?\r\n\r\n\r\nAdult mental health is a person's emotional, psychological and social health in adulthood. It affects the way people think, feel, behave, deal with stress, form relationships, make decisions and deal with daily problems. Mental wellbeing contributes to overall wellbeing and quality of life. [1]\r\n\r\n2. Why is mental health important for adults?\r\n\r\nMental health has a significant impact on nearly every facet of adult life, such as work performance, relationships, parenting, physical health, sleep, emotional resiliency and decision making. A healthy mind is a key component to coping with everyday life. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\n3. What are the most common mental health concerns in adults?\r\n\r\n\r\nStress, anxiety, depression, burnout, sleep issues, panic attacks, OCD, emotional exhaustion, relationship issues, work-related stress are among the common concerns. Each individual has a different experience and if symptoms persist, it should be assessed by a professional. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n4. How do I know if I should seek professional mental health support?\r\n\r\n\r\nIt's worth talking to a professional if emotional issues last for a few weeks, if they affect your work, relationships or daily life, if they are not easy to manage yourself, or if they bring a lot of problems. Assessment at an early stage can aid in determining factors and support. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\n5. What is the difference between stress and anxiety?\r\n\r\nStress is often an adaptive response to a life situation, for example work, finances or family responsibilities, and therefore is often improved by altering the situation. Anxiety can be characterized as an excessive worry or fear that persists even when there is no stressor present. If anxiety persists, it is advisable that a qualified health care provider determine its source. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\n6. Can chronic stress affect physical health?\r\n\r\nYes. Stress can lead to headaches, muscle tension, stomach upset, weak focus and sleep issues, decreased concentration. When physical symptoms are ongoing, it is always important to have the symptoms assessed by a trained health care provider to detect any medical issues. [1][3]\r\n\r\n\r\n7. What are the signs of depression in adults?\r\n\r\nSymptoms may include prolonged depression, lack of interest, diminished energy, changes in eating or sleeping habits, trouble focusing, hopelessness or loss of interest. If any of these symptoms persist or impact daily functioning, the symptoms should be assessed by a professional. [1]\r\n\r\n8. What is burnout?\r\n\r\n\r\nBurnout is the feeling of emotional, physical and mental fatigue that can occur as a result of continuing stress or caring for others. Symptoms include ongoing fatigue, loss of motivation, emotional disconnect and struggling with everyday tasks. [2]\r\n\r\n\r\n9. Can poor sleep affect mental health?\r\n\r\n\r\nYes. There is a strong link between sleep and mental health. Not sleeping well can affect feelings, focus, emotional control, stress and happiness. If sleep problems continue, talk to a trained health care provider. [4]\r\n\r\n\r\n10. What is an adult mental health assessment?\r\n\r\nAn adult mental health assessment is a structured assessment covering emotional wellbeing, stress levels, mood, behaviour, sleep, lifestyle, relationships, work-related issues and mental health. The assessment is used to determine strengths, challenges and next steps for personalized support.\r\n\r\n\r\n11. How does Manovaidya support adult mental health?\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya the support starts with understanding the individual and not only his/her symptoms. We guide individual to understand emotional wellbeing, lifestyle, behaviour, stress and overall mental health in a structured way through Neuro-Ayurveda Development System and personalised guidance.\r\n\r\n12. What is the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System?\r\n\r\nThe Neuro-Ayurveda Development System is Manovaidya’s 5 pillar system designed to integrate the four aspects of Brain Nourishment, Gut Response, Neural Network Development and Sensory Integration and Behaviour Guidance under a single umbrella, giving a holistic understanding of mental wellbeing. It offers an overview and complete evaluation with tailored support. [3][5][6]\r\n\r\n13. When should I seek urgent mental health support?\r\n\r\nIf you have thoughts of self harm or suicide, if you are unable to keep yourself safe, if you have tried to hurt yourself, if you experience hallucinations, severe confusion, or if you feel you are an immediate danger to yourself or others, it is very important that you get medical or emergency mental health care right away. There should be no delay in emergency care in these cases. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\n15. Can work-related stress affect mental health?\r\n\r\nYes. Persistent stress at work can lead to anxiety, burnout, decreased motivation, trouble sleeping, emotional fatigue, and problems maintaining balance in your work and personal life. It is important to respond to these worries early in order to enhance emotional health and functioning. [2]\r\n\r\n\r\n16. Why should I choose Manovaidya for adult mental health care?\r\n\r\nIn Manovaidya we are very interested in the total emotional wellbeing of each person, using structured assessments, personalized guidance and the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System. We take a holistic view of emotional health, lifestyle, behaviour and long-term wellbeing and work with individuals to help them build resilience, enhance emotional balance and help them to develop healthier coping mechanisms.\r\n\r\nReferences\r\n[1] World Health Organization (WHO) — Mental Health: Strengthening Our Response\r\nhttps://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/mental-health-strengthening-our-response\r\n[2] World Health Organization (WHO) — Burn-out as an Occupational Phenomenon (ICD-11)\r\nhttps://www.who.int/standards/classifications/frequently-asked-questions/burn-out-an-occupational-phenomenon\r\n[3] National Library of Medicine (PMC) — Gut Microbiota’s Effect on Mental Health: The Gut-Brain Axis\r\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5641835/\r\n[4] National Library of Medicine (PMC) — The Gut–Brain–Circadian Axis in Anxiety and Depression: A Critical Review\r\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12611926/\r\n[5] Ministry of AYUSH, Government of India — AYUSH Research Portal: Evidence-Based Research in Ayurveda and AYUSH Systems\r\nhttps://arp.ayush.gov.in/\r\n[6] Ministry of AYUSH, Government of India — NAMASTE Portal: Standardized Ayurveda Terminologies and Morbidity Codes\r\nhttps://namaste.ayush.gov.in/sat_Ayurveda";
